[profiles.guide]
notes = '''Hold {select} and {start} together to pause the gyro while you reposition the controller. Hold {start} to switch the gyro off or on, and hold {r3} to recenter it.
Flick stick: push the right stick {rs} toward where you want to face and the view turns to it; turn it around the rim to keep turning. The gyro aims up, down and finely.
{start} (Escape) opens the game's menu and closes the inventory and the map. The game saves on the server, so there's no quick save.
{south} interacts: loot, open doors, talk to vendors, board the helicopter. Hold {south} to sprint. {east} jumps and vaults. {west} reloads and a long press of {west} switches the fire mode. {north} switches the weapon light or laser, and a long press of {north} lowers or raises night vision.
{l3} crouches and a long press of {l3} goes prone. {r3} is melee. {left} and {right} lean while held, and {up} and {down} turn the mouse wheel to step through weapons and pick options in the interaction list.
Hold {lb} for the weapon ring, aiming with the right stick {rs}: primary, second primary, sidearm, melee and grenade. {rb} throws a grenade.
{select} opens the inventory, and a long press of {select} the map. In the inventory and map the right stick moves the pointer, {rt} clicks and {lt} right-clicks; drag items by holding {rt}.
Chat needs typing: open the on-screen keyboard with {guide} + {west}.
The game uses Easy Anti-Cheat; the pad reaches it as an ordinary keyboard and mouse.
These keys are written from memory and not checked in the game (fire mode, weapon light, night vision, grenade, melee, prone and the weapon slots especially). Compare them with Settings → Controls and change the buttons here to match. The executable name comes from Discord's detection list, which keeps it under a Win64 folder. The gyro's real-world turn of 8000 pixels at the default mouse sensitivity is guessed, not measured.'''

